[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Message Queues
PREFIX: ZEP-SRS-17-

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: software_requirements.sgra

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
<<<

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Message Queue Definition and Initialization

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-8
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Static message queue definition
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide a mechanism to define and initialize a message queue at
compile time, specifying the message size and maximum number of queued messages.
<<<
USER_STORY: >>>
As a Zephyr RTOS user I want to asynchronously pass fixed-size data items between threads
and interrupt service routines using a bounded FIFO buffer.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-9
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Runtime message queue initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to initialize a message queue at run time
using a caller-provided buffer, specifying the message size and maximum number of
queued messages.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-10
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Heap-allocated message queue initialization
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to initialize a message queue at run time
by allocating the required buffer from the kernel heap, specifying the message size and
maximum number of queued messages.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-11
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Message queue cleanup
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to release resources associated with a
heap-allocated message queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Sending Messages

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-12
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Enqueue a message
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to add a message to the back of a message
queue, blocking the calling thread if the queue is full until space becomes available
or a timeout expires.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-13
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Enqueue a message at the front
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to add a message to the front of a message
queue, making it the next item to be retrieved, without blocking.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-14
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Send timeout behavior
STATEMENT: >>>
When enqueuing a message times out because the queue remains full, the Zephyr RTOS
shall return a timeout error code to the calling thread.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Receiving Messages

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-15
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Dequeue a message
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to remove the first message from a message
queue and copy it to a caller-supplied buffer, blocking the calling thread if the queue
is empty until a message arrives or a timeout expires.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-16
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Peek at the first message
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to copy the first message from a message
queue into a caller-supplied buffer without removing it from the queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-17
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Peek at a message by index
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to copy a message at a specified index
within a message queue into a caller-supplied buffer without removing it from the queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-18
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Receive timeout behaviour
STATEMENT: >>>
When dequeuing from an empty message queue times out, the Zephyr RTOS shall return a
timeout error code to the calling thread.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[[/SECTION]]

[[SECTION]]
TITLE: Message Queue Inspection

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-19
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Query number of free slots
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to query the number of unused message slots
remaining in a message queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-20
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Query number of queued messages
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to query the number of messages currently
stored in a message queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-21
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Query message queue attributes
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to retrieve the static attributes of a
message queue, including message size and maximum queue depth.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: ZEP-SRS-17-22
STATUS: Draft
TYPE: Functional
COMPONENT: Message Queues
TITLE: Purge all messages
STATEMENT: >>>
The Zephyr RTOS shall provide an interface to discard all messages currently stored in
a message queue and unblock any threads waiting to send to the queue.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: ZEP-SYRS-31

[[/SECTION]]
